      "role": "user",
      "content": "im having a really hard time trying to map out these patterns i keep getting. it's like im seeing these sudden spikes in probability for specific events right before they happen, almost like a sensory input but it's clearly mathematical. like a sudden jump from 5% to 88% certainty in a split second for something totally random. i want to try and build a formal predictive model to track these temporal spikes so i can actually quantify them. can you help me figure out a way to log and structure these intuitive probability shifts?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
